  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;NOTE A &amp;#8211; ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Organization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;White Cliffs Pipeline, L.L.C. (&amp;#8220;White Cliffs&amp;#8221;) is a Delaware limited liability company &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;formed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; on January 26, 2007.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; White Cliffs is a joint venture owned 5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;4.33&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;% by ET CC Holdings, L.L.C., an indirect &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;wholly-owned&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP (&amp;#8220;Energy Transfer&amp;#8221;), 35.67% by Plains Pipeline, LP, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;10% by Anadarko Wattenberg Company, LLC c/o Western Midstream Partners, LP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;White Cliffs is principally engaged in the transportation of crude oil and natural gas liquids (&amp;#8220;NGLs&amp;#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; White Cliffs&amp;#8217; operations and reporting are divided into the following pipeline systems:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Crude Oil Pipeline System. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;White Cliffs provides crude oil transportation services on approximately 527 miles of 12-inch diameter common carrier trunk pipelines that originate in Platteville, Colorado and terminate at a storage facility in Cushing, Oklahoma. This crude pipeline system connects the DJ Basin to the Cushing, Oklahoma market.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;NGL Pipeline System. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;White Cliffs established NGL service from Platteville, Colorado to Cushing, Oklahoma on pipeline facilities parallel to the White Cliffs Crude Oil Pipeline system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;. White Cliffs&amp;#8217; crude oil and NGL transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") and various state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting practices, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Basis of Presentation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;#8220;GAAP&amp;#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;the statement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; of cash flows and (2) use of FERC approved depreciation rates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;These interim financial statements should be read in conjunction with the financial statements and notes thereto contained in the White Cliffs FERC Form 6 for the year &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; December 31, 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;. The financial statements are unaudited, but in the opinion of management, all adjustments have been made that are necessary to fairly state the financial position, results of operations and cash flows for the periods presented. Certain information and notes that would substantially duplicate the disclosures contained in the most recent FERC Form 6 have been omitted.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; widows: 0; orphans: 0; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
